    "title": "37-Year-Old Shoved Onto Harlem Subway Tracks, Riders Pull Him to Safety - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Nolan Keegan ,\n21 hours ago A 37-year-old man was shoved off the platform and onto the subway tracks at the 125th Street station in Harlem on Tuesday night, following an argument with another rider that sent him tumbling onto the roadbed just before an oncoming train. Fellow commuters pulled him back onto the platform before a train arrived, and he was rushed to Harlem Hospital in stable condition after avoiding contact with the third rail. The man who shoved him fled the station on foot, and police have not made an arrest. Read full article\n9",
